{"url": "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/ceg/research/graduate-school/", "final_url": "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/ceg/research/graduate-school/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "Graduate School CEG\nActivate high contrast\nTo main content\nHome\nStories of Science\nEducation\nBachelor programmes\nMaster programmes\nOnline education\nMinors\nStudent Stories\nPostgraduates\nResearch\nStories of Science\nProfessors\nDelft Research Initiatives\nResearch institutes\nSector plan\nGraduate School\nPublications\nResearch Assessments\nCooperation\nStrategic partnership\nInternship or graduation\nContribution to education\nCurrent\nLatest news\nAgenda\nIn the media\nCEG on Social Media\nAwards and publications\nPress room\nAbout the faculty\nDean\nDepartments\nLaboratories\nAlumni\nAssociations and societies\nWorking at our faculty\nEDI & Academic Culture\nFacts and Figures\nContact and map\nSearch\nHome\nStories of Science\nEducation\nMenu openen\nBachelor programmes\nMaster programmes\nOnline education\nMinors\nStudent Stories\nPostgraduates\nResearch\nMenu openen\nStories of Science\nProfessors\nDelft Research Initiatives\nResearch institutes\nSector plan\nGraduate School\nPublications\nResearch Assessments\nCooperation\nMenu openen\nStrategic partnership\nInternship or graduation\nContribution to education\nCurrent\nMenu openen\nLatest news\nAgenda\nIn the media\nCEG on Social Media\nAwards and publications\nPress room\nAbout the faculty\nMenu openen\nDean\nDepartments\nLaboratories\nAlumni\nAssociations and societies\nWorking at our faculty\nEDI & Academic Culture\nFacts and Figures\nContact and map\nDit is het social media blok\nlinkedin\ninstagram\nyoutube\nwhatsapp\nwhatsapp\nNederlands\nActivate high contrast\nClose menu\nSearch\nClose search\nCivil Engineering and Geosciences\nResearch\nGraduate School\nGraduate School CEG\nWelcome to the CEG Graduate School\nThe Graduate School offers a stimulating environment for you if you wish to obtain a doctoral degree with the highest possible value for your career. You will have the opportunity to immerse in high-impact research projects across a variety of disciplines and to benefit from close interactions with world-class researchers and teachers.\nOur offer\nAn inspiring research environment\nAn excellent team of supervisors that will guide you through\nThe ability to take charge of your own personal development in the form of a skills program that you can tailor to your own personal needs\nAre you the brilliant engineer we are looking for?\nNot one single day passes without being in close contact with the research area of our Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences. Catching a train or car, crossing a bridge, taking a shower or flushing the toilet, or just watching safely the sea behind the dykes, are common daily activities for which a sound civil infrastructure is indispensable. In a rapidly changing world our demand to our infrastructure is drastically changing meanwhile it receives our blind trust! To sustain our societal comfort we need to understand how our climate is changing and what are the impacts so we can anticipate on due time. Energy supply without greenhouse gas emissions and resource recycling will become panacea in our future world.\nBrilliant engineers and scientists, like you!, are challenged to contribute to develop our future, sustaining our societal comfort as we know it. Unveiling the future necessities, pinpointing the knowledge gaps, managing your own research, unravelling engineering complexities, delivering high-quality results, and being in contact with practitioners, is a PhD life at our faculty. You will be trained being a world-class professional in science and engineering of societal relevance.\nWe offer up to date high quality research facilities as well making use of abundant satellite data. Equipped with high-level personal skills you will hold a key position after your graduation. This is what society expects from you when you leave us again, and this is what we offer in your PhD trajectory. If you are challenged by what we are offering then we hope to welcome you soon as PhD candidate in our midst.\nProf.dr.ir. Serge Hoogendoorn\nDirector Graduate School CEG\nFor those who have already started a PhD position at the Faculty of CEG: please visit for more information the intranet website of the CEG Graduate School.\nInformation for current PhD candidates\n(login)\nShare this page:\nFacebook\nLinkedin\nTwitter\nEmail\nWhatsApp\nShare this page\nOpen menu\nGraduate School\nStarting a PhD at CEG\nPhD or EngD?\nAdmission\nFees and Funding\nContact\nPhD Council\nFaculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences\nDit is het social media blok\nlinkedin\ninstagram\nyoutube\nwhatsapp\nwhatsapp\nBuilding 23\nStevinweg 1\n2628 CN Delft\nTel: + 31 15 27 89802\nStories of Science\nContact and map\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy statement\nActivate high contrast\nHome\nStories of Science\nEducation\nBachelor programmes\nMaster programmes\nOnline education\nMinors\nStudent Stories\nPostgraduates\nResearch\nStories of Science\nProfessors\nDelft Research Initiatives\nResearch institutes\nSector plan\nGraduate School\nPublications\nResearch Assessments\nCooperation\nStrategic partnership\nInternship or graduation\nContribution to education\nCurrent\nLatest news\nAgenda\nIn the media\nCEG on Social Media\nAwards and publications\nPress room\nAbout the faculty\nDean\nDepartments\nLaboratories\nAlumni\nAssociations and societies\nWorking at our faculty\nEDI & Academic Culture\nFacts and Figures\nContact and map\nSearch", "links": [["To main content", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/ceg/research/graduate-school/#main"], ["TU Delft homepage", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/"], ["Home", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/ceg"], ["Stories of Science", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/ceg/research/stories-of-science"], ["Education", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/ceg/education"], ["Bachelor programmes", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/ceg/education/